## Why This Is Asked

This question probes mastery of runtime extensibility, safe composition of hot-pluggable components, and streaming guarantees in a real-world UI analytics context.

## Key Concepts

- Registry of plugins and factories
- Pipeline composition and deterministic order
- Per-event isolation and context cloning
- Controlled parallelism and backpressure

## Code Example

```javascript
interface Processor {
  process(ctx: any, data: any): Promise<any>;
}
class ProcessorRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, () => Processor>();
  register(name: string, factory: () => Processor) { this.map.set(name, factory); }
  create(name: string): Processor { const f = this.map.get(name); if (!f) throw new Error(`Unknown processor: ${name}`); return f(); }
}
class Pipeline {
  constructor(private steps: string[], private registry: ProcessorRegistry) {}
  async run(ctx: any, data: any) {
    let out = data;
    for (const name of this.steps) {
      const p = this.registry.create(name);
      out = await p.process(ctx, out);
    }
    return out;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you design error handling, retries, and circuit breaking across processors?
- How would you support dynamic reordering without disrupting in-flight events?

